question:
Why does the last line produce a type error?
```ts
function printText(s: string, alignment: "left" | "right" | "center") {}

let a = "left";
printText("Hello", a); // error
```

explanation:
```ts
function doSomething(x: string | null) {
  if (x === null) {
    // handle it
  } else {
    console.log(x.toUpperCase()); // OK — narrowed to string
  }
}
```
With `strictNullChecks` off, forgetting a null check is invisible to the compiler — a major source of bugs. Turning it on is always recommended.

