explanation:
```ts
function log(msg: string): void { console.log(msg); }
function safeParse(s: string): unknown { return JSON.parse(s); }
function fail(msg: string): never { throw new Error(msg); }
```
Unlike `any`, an `unknown` return forces callers to check the value before using it. `never` also feeds control-flow analysis: code after a call to a `never`-returning function is unreachable, and in exhaustive switches the leftover type is `never`.

