What is the type of `strs` inside the `if` block?
```ts
function printAll(strs: string | string[] | null) {
  if (typeof strs === "object") {
    // here
  }
}
```

explanation:
```ts
function printAll(strs: string | string[] | null) {
  if (strs && typeof strs === "object") {
    for (const s of strs) console.log(s);
  } else if (typeof strs === "string") {
    console.log(strs);
  }
}
```
Wrapping the whole body in `if (strs)` instead would silently skip the empty string — a valid input. Prefer explicit checks (`!= null`) when falsy values are meaningful.

